+// -------------------------------------------------------------------------
+// Debug taps: inside the CORTEXA53 macro itself, along the instruction-
+// fetch-request generation path. Every tap so far (cpu_axi_arvalid_dbg,
+// NIC-400 taps) sits *outside* the macro, at its external ARVALIDM pin -
+// nothing between the IFU deciding to fetch and that pin has ever been
+// directly observed. XMR straight into the licensed-but-unencrypted RTL's
+// own internal port/signal names, same pattern as the clock-gate taps
+// above; instance hierarchy confirmed against the routed netlist first
