+// 2026-08-28: with clock (core0_clk_ever_toggled_dbg) and core reset
+// (ncorereset_dbg) both confirmed reliably healthy on hardware, ARVALID
+// still never asserts - the blocker is further downstream. Traced:
+// ifu_arvalid_o requires the prefetch buffer to leave its post-reset
+// stopped state (ca53ifu_pf.v: stop_pfb resets to 1 and only clears via
+// dpu_pfu_force from the DPU), which requires the DPU's own self-
+// triggering reset-exception FSM (ca53dpu_exception.v) to walk all the
+// way from ST_EXPT_RESET0 to ST_EXPT_IDLE. That FSM can stall forever at
+// ST_EXPT_ISS_FORCEOP if fpu_interlock_iss_i (tied to the separately
+// power-gated NEON/ADVSIMD pipeline, confirmed present via UPF power-
+// domain PDCPUADVSIMD) stays stuck asserted - a plausible, previously
+// unobserved blocker even though the NEON PPU's own Q-channel handshake
+// (CPU_NEON_qreqn/qacceptn/qactive) has separately already been confirmed
+// completing every cycle (that only proves power-sequencing completed,
+// not that this internal hazard-tracking signal behaves correctly).
+// expt_idle_o is the FSM's own "reached IDLE" output - directly answers
+// whether the reset-exception sequence that ungates the first fetch ever
